From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_DRAIN_ON_GROWTH=1 or =<MiB>, the pressure drain runs once the allocator has grown that much since the last drain, and deleted buffers go once the GPU is past them instead of after 8 frame ends (off unless set)

Why: at the load past Ocarina's field about 2.5 GiB of graphics memory arrives within a second and the
pool hits zero. In that first second another 966 MiB was made and freed again by one late drain
(run1545, EDEN_UP_PRESSURE_DRAIN 12): 689 MiB of buffers already deleted, waiting for 8 frame ends
inside a load frame that lasts seconds, and 276 MiB of staging. The drain came late because
PressureDrainLook looks only every 256 draws and at least 50 ms apart; allocator use had reached 1972
MiB from a 639 MiB low by then.

What, with EDEN_UP_DRAIN_ON_GROWTH=1 (256 MiB) or =<MiB> (32 to 65535; anything else off; read once):
- renderer_vulkan/pressure_drain.h (GrowthState, GrowthDue) and vk_rasterizer.cpp PressureDrainLook:
  between the 256-draw looks, every 16th draw or dispatch reads MemoryAllocator::UsedBytes. Once use is
  the switch's amount over its lowest since the last drain, the look comes at once (not 50 ms after the
  last) and drains at once, whatever waits and however much room the pool has, at most every
  EDEN_UP_DRAIN_AT_AREA_GAP_MS (100). The drain itself is the pressure drain's own (flush, wait at most
  EDEN_UP_PRESSURE_DRAIN_MS, release; GPU-behind and conditional-rendering rules unchanged). Needs
  EDEN_UP_PRESSURE_DRAIN=1 (with =2 only frame ends look; unset: no drains, only the part below).
- buffer_cache/pending_destroy.h (DrainOnGrowthBytes, TickedDestroyList), buffer_cache_base.h,
  buffer_cache.h DeleteBuffer: a deleted buffer goes into a TickedDestroyList instead of the
  DelayedDestructionRing. At a safe point of the recording thread (RasterizerVulkan::TickFrame after
  the caches' TickFrame, the 16-draw look before a draw is set up, and a drain whose wait ran out) every
  unstamped deleted buffer gets the tick being recorded then, and the stamped ones the GPU is past are
  destroyed (BufferCache::ReleaseDeletedPassed: one IsFreeNow for the oldest, IsFree for the rest; no
  flush, no wait). Not while the guest's conditional rendering is on (its predicate buffer, as the
  drain), and not in the 16-draw look with EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW=1 (its delta draws keep texture buffer
  views until a frame end or a drain). A drain that reaches its tick destroys all of them, as before.
  At the latest a deleted buffer goes where and when the ring would have freed it: BufferCache::
  TickFrame destroys, stamped or not, those deleted TICKS_TO_DESTROY (8) frame ends ago
  (TickedDestroyList::ReleaseAged), so with conditional rendering on nothing waits longer than T185.
  DeletedWaiting, ForEachDeleted, ReportMemory and ReleasePendingBuffers count the list too.
Lines (stderr): at boot "EDEN_UP_DRAIN_ON_GROWTH on: a drain once the allocator has grown N MiB over
its low since the last drain (...); deleted buffers go once the GPU is past the tick stamped on them at
a frame end, a 16-draw look or a drain, at the latest 8 frame ends later as before"; per growth drain (first 64, then every 16th)
"EDEN_UP_DRAIN_ON_GROWTH drain G (drain D, in a frame|at a frame end): allocator use U MiB, X over its
low of L MiB since the last drain; waited W ms, the GPU finished|did not finish; F MiB freed (S MiB of
it staging; B deleted buffers M MiB by the GPU's tick without the wait); deleted buffers before: n, m
MiB; largest free piece before P MiB; T MiB freed by growth drains so far"; every 10 s while any went
"EDEN_UP_DRAIN_ON_GROWTH_10S B deleted buffers M MiB destroyed once the GPU was past them (not 8 frame
ends later), A at the 8 frame ends as before; T MiB by tick so far; waiting now: n buffers m MiB".

Unset: the switch is read once (rasterizer constructor); PressureDrainLook returns at the same draws
as T185, the 50 ms gate and every drain rule are T185's, DeleteBuffer pushes to the ring as T185, and
the list stays empty (every count adds 0): as T185. No translation id input is touched (none of these
files is reached from src/shader_recompiler or in tools/gen-translation-id.py's SINGLE list), no wait
site line is added to a cost file, no anchor line changes, and the name is not in TranslationSwitches:
KEEPS THE STORE.
